From 1fda54b32a59a1e62dd25b007c1535dfbc7d89f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruilin Gao <ruiling@andrew.cmu.edu>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:16:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [rollout] fix: fall back to a default Continuous Token
 builder when a required token is missing

DeepSeek-R1 distills keep Qwen model_type values (qwen2/qwen3) but ship
DeepSeek's tokenizer, which renames <|im_end|> to its own end-of-sentence
marker. Since #6804 the builder family is an exact model_type lookup, so
QwenContinuousTokenBuilder.__init__ raises "Tokenizer does not define
required token '<|im_end|>'" before any rollout starts (#7637).

With auto inference, treat a builder whose required token is missing like
an unregistered model_type and fall back to the default behavior with a
warning. The fallback is a dedicated subclass carrying the synthetic
tool-call arguments as the JSON string form of #7630, because these
checkpoints' templates splice arguments in by string concatenation; the
base class keeps the mapping form, which registered templates such as
Qwen3.5, MiniMax-M2 and GLM-4.7 render with .items(). An explicitly
requested family still raises.
---
